  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "Suppose $r$ is a real number such that $|r|<1$. Determine a formula for\n$$r+2r^2+3r^3+4r^4+\\cdots.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{r}{(1-r)^2}$.\n\nMultiply the sum by $r$ and subtract to obtain a geometric series.",
      "worked": "Let $S$ denote the infinite sum. Multiply by $r$ and subtract:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nS&=r+2r^2+3r^3+4r^4+\\cdots\\\\\nrS&=r^2+2r^3+3r^4+4r^5+\\cdots\\\\\nS-rS&=r+r^2+r^3+r^4+\\cdots\\\\\nS-rS&=\\frac{r}{1-r}\\\\\n(1-r)S&=\\frac{r}{1-r}\\\\\nS&=\\frac{r}{(1-r)^2}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe geometric sum is valid because $|r|<1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
